  "id": "auditory-continuous-performance-test",
  "term": "Auditory Continuous Performance Test",
  "definition": "The Auditory Continuous Performance Test is a diagnostic test used to look for problems with auditory attention. A person listens to single words and responds when a target word is heard, which can help in identifying attention deficits such as ADD or ADHD in children ages 6 to 11.",
